Author: Abhinav S V <abhinavsv3@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Sep 25 22:46:13 2026 -0700

    report --markdown and --json, and a badge command for READMEs
    
    The report was an ANSI table. The place people want to put a result is
    a pull request comment or a README, where escape codes are garbage.
    
    --markdown writes the model table, the F2P-only comparison and a
    collapsed per-task grid as GitHub Markdown; --json writes the summarised
    rows. Either takes - for stdout, in which case the terminal table stays
    off it so the output is the artifact.
    
    groundhog badge writes a shields.io endpoint file:
    
      ![agent pass rate](https://img.shields.io/endpoint?url=.../badge.json)
    
    It refuses to show a number for a model the harness could not read. A
    percentage in a README is the most context-free place a number can
    live, and a wrong one lives there forever.
    
    Closes #28
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

